# ship-feature — example configuration.
#
# Copy to ~/.config/ship-feature/config and edit. The `ship-feature` CLI reads this file as plain
# `KEY=value` lines and honors the SHIP_FEATURE_* keys below — it is NEVER shell-`source`d, so nothing
# here is executed. Environment variables of the same name take precedence over this file.
#
# The values below are the built-in defaults. This example file is TRACKED and public; put your real
# values only in the copy at ~/.config/ship-feature/config, which is gitignored.

# Where the workflow creates git worktrees (relative to the repo root). Default matches the CLI.
SHIP_FEATURE_WORKTREE_ROOT=.claude/worktrees

# Marker directory that must be git-excluded so it never shows up in `git status`.
SHIP_FEATURE_EXCLUDE_MARKER=.claude/

# The cross-review quorum: the agents you actually have installed. When set, `ship-feature relay`
# injects it as --reviewers (so a missing agent fails the round instead of silently thinning the panel).
# LEFT UNSET by default on purpose — uncomment and list ONLY the agents you have, or a fresh install
# would force a quorum you can't satisfy and every review round would fail.
# SHIP_FEATURE_REVIEWERS=claude,codex,cursor

# Optional: a DIFFERENT (usually smaller) default panel for `ship-feature plan-review` — the cheap
# read-only plan gate often wants fewer reviewers than the full PR cross-review. Falls back to
# SHIP_FEATURE_REVIEWERS when unset. Override per-run with `--reviewers`.
# SHIP_FEATURE_PLAN_REVIEWERS=claude,codex

# Path to a PRIVATE, newline-delimited deny-list for scripts/scan-personal-data.sh. Each line is a
# literal string that must NEVER appear in the public repo (real project slugs, bundle-id prefixes,
# home paths, internal hostnames). Keep this file OUT of git.
SHIP_FEATURE_DENYLIST=/path/to/your/denylist.txt

# Escape hatch, ENV-ONLY (export it — it is NOT read from this file): set SHIP_FEATURE_ALLOW_BEHIND=1 to
# let `ship-feature preflight` proceed when your branch is behind/diverged from the default branch.

# Per-reviewer timeout for `ship-feature plan-review`, in seconds. ENV-ONLY (not read from this file);
# falls back to PR_RELAY_AGENT_TIMEOUT, then 300. e.g. export SHIP_FEATURE_PLAN_TIMEOUT=480

# Model for the `cursor` plan reviewer. Default: composer-2.5, Cursor's own model -- Cursor-branded
# quota pool, and not Claude, GPT, Codex or Grok, so every reviewer on the panel stays on the model
# its own vendor built. ENV-ONLY (not read from this
# file — it is outside the SHIP_FEATURE_* namespace, so load_config never sees it). The name has no
# SHIP_FEATURE_ prefix on purpose: pr-review-relay reads the SAME variable, because it describes your
# Cursor account rather than either tool, and one export should configure both.
# It is pinned rather than left on cursor-agent's own "Auto" default, which routes to the frontier
# models and may pick a Claude one — plan-review would then have Claude grading a plan Claude wrote,
# while the panel reports an independent "Cursor" reviewer. (Auto also bills Cursor's small "Other
# Models" quota instead of the larger Cursor-branded pool.)
# `cursor-agent --list-models` shows what your account offers. Pick something OUTSIDE the families
# already on your panel: setting this back to `auto`, to a claude-* id while Claude writes your
# plans, or to a cursor-grok-* id while grok45high reviews alongside it, all collapse two nominally
# independent seats onto one model family. The override is for a retired model id.
# e.g. export CURSOR_REVIEW_MODEL=cursor-grok-4.5-high
